# Trims the build context uploaded to Cloud Build. The Dockerfile copies only
# package*.json, src/, and terraform/, so nothing here can reach the image —
# this is about upload size and cache churn.
#
# Do NOT ignore package-lock.json: `npm ci` needs it, and without it the build
# silently falls back to re-resolving the dependency ranges.
node_modules
npm-debug.log
.git

# Terraform working state: provider plugins are hundreds of MB, and tfstate or
# generated tfvars could carry real infrastructure details into the context.
# `.terraform.lock.hcl` is deliberately NOT ignored — it is committed to pin
# provider versions, and the runner's `terraform init` needs it in the image.
**/.terraform
**/terraform.tfstate*
**/terraform.tfvars.json

# Never copied into the image.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
README.md
tsconfig.json
